# Every cluster call the pod daemon's kubectl commands make, one line per distinct
# call as `verb resource`. Every call is in the gt namespace. The groups below say
# which command each line serves, read from the code:
#
# patch deployments: podDaemonSwap.Apply in internal/cmd/update_pod_swap.go, the
#   strategic patch of the daemon's Deployment (kubectl patch deployment/<name>).
#
# get deployments, list deployments, watch deployments: podDaemonSwap.Apply's
#   rollout wait (kubectl rollout status deployment/<name>). The get also serves the
#   Deployment read in the exec below.
#
# get pods, list pods, create pods/exec: podDaemonCommit in
#   internal/cmd/update_pod_probe.go (kubectl exec deployment/<name> -- gt version).
#   The exec reads the pod it runs in, lists the pods the Deployment selects, and
#   creates the exec.
patch deployments
get deployments
list deployments
watch deployments
get pods
list pods
create pods/exec
